         By default the channel volumes are used.
 
+``audiotrack``
+    Android AudioTrack audio output driver.
+
+    The following global options are supported by this audio output:
+
+    ``--audiotrack-stream-silence-limit=<0-86400>``
+        With ``--audio-stream-silence=yes``, a passthrough (bitstream) track is
+        kept running while the player has no audio for it - across pauses,
+        seeks and underruns - by feeding it silence: a silent frame of the
+        codec for raw AC-3, E-AC-3 and DTS at 48 kHz, zero words for the
+        IEC 61937 carrier. A receiver that would otherwise lose the stream and
+        lock on it again on resume stays locked. Raw TrueHD, raw DTS-HD and
+        raw tracks at other sample rates get no silence and drop the stream as
+        without the option; a PCM track is padded with silence by the player
+        itself.
+
+        Since the track is not flushed on a seek or a pause either, whatever
+        it holds plays out first. The option therefore also caps the audio
+        queued in a passthrough track: while the playback head moves, no
+        more is read from the player once 500 ms is queued (a raw track's
+        byte budget would otherwise hold 1.28 s of a 192 kb/s AC-3 stream);
+        a head that stands still gets the track filled.
+
+        This option bounds each feed: once the queued audio has drained to
+        300 ms the silence starts, and after this many seconds of it the track
+        is paused and flushed, so the output goes to standby and the bitstream
+        stops. It starts again with the next audio. ``0`` feeds for as long as
+        the player has no audio. The value is read when the audio output
+        opens (default: 60).
+
 ``sdl``
     SDL 2.0+ audio output driver. Should work on any platform supported by SDL
     2.0, but may require the ``SDL_AUDIODRIVER`` environment variable to be set
